From 48c3dd77e791c8220a4589599bd80c4c1462e697 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 16:07:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/32] feat(desktop): web build-stamp self-compare with resume
 auto-reload
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

F4d: write-build-stamp.mjs also emits public/build-stamp.json (buildId =
commit+builtAt); vite's publicDir copies it into dist-web after the
emptyOutDir wipe and the same file feeds the __HERMES_BUILD_STAMP__ define,
so the embedded constant and the served stamp compare equal by
construction. Electron builds copy the file into dist/ inertly.

User addendum B: the web build re-fetches ${BASE_URL}build-stamp.json
(relative — resolves under /app/, never the dashboard catch-all) on load
AND on visibilitychange->visible, because a home-screen WKWebView resumes
without navigation so HTML cache headers never run. A mismatch
auto-reloads ONCE per remote stamp (sessionStorage guard against loops)
and falls back to a manual translated update pill when the reload already
happened. No-op in the Electron build.
